menu "SolarPay"

config SOLARPAY_TEST_HARNESS
    bool "Enable the serial test harness (SP_TEST_*)"
    default n
    help
      Adds SP_TEST_IMPACT, SP_TEST_BTN and SP_TEST_STATE to the serial console
      so an automated harness on a laptop can drive the pairing and approval
      flow that normally needs a physical knock and a physical button press.

      This exists because the two acts that gate a payment -- knocking the
      badges together and pressing A -- have no other injection point, which
      makes the end-to-end flow untestable without a pair of hands. It drives
      the real state machine and the real ESP-NOW radio; only the accelerometer
      and 74HC165 drivers are bypassed, so those still need a manual pass.

      SP_TEST_BTN reaches the same approve() that the A button reaches. Shipping
      a build with this enabled would let anything that can write to the USB
      console approve a payment. Default n, and it must stay that way: turn it
      on only through sdkconfig.test, never sdkconfig.defaults.

endmenu
